 "description": "Perle IOLAN SCG50 R console server, 1U, with 48 RJ45 RS-232 serial ports in all three of its G16 module bays. It has dual AC power and two network pairs of RJ45 and SFP. The front carries the display, the keypad, the power button, the ready lamp and the card slot. It also has the RJ45 and micro-USB admin ports, two USB 3.0 ports and the reset hole. The rear carries the network pairs at the left, the module bays and the two inlets, each with a rocker switch. Modelled as the dual-AC build with no cellular parts, as the R/U product page lists none.",
 "format": 1,
 "gaps": [
  {
   "note": "The 3 fitted modules are drawn as the chassis's own jacks: no document dimensions a G16 module or its face plate, so no module is modelled and no bay is declared where one is fitted (a bay may not overlap a placement). The three bays take the 16-port RS-232 RJ45, USB or multi-protocol RJ45 G16 module in consecutive order from Bay 1 (guide pages 9 and 10); that rule is words only and no tool checks it.",
   "reason": "needs-drawing",
   "scope": [
    "rear"
   ],
   "wanted": "a dimensioned drawing of a G16 module and a larger straight-on photograph of the rear.",
   "what": "g16-modules"
  },
  {
   "note": "The lower view of the drawing shows a field of vent slots and a pattern of screw holes, undimensioned, and the guide does not say which side it is. The two sides draw the envelope only.",
   "reason": "needs-drawing",
   "scope": [
    "left",
    "right"
   ],
   "wanted": "the side view of guide page 35 read for its vent slots and holes, which the drawing does not dimension.",
   "what": "side-vents"
  },
  {
   "note": "The page 9 photograph shows an orange trim line and diagonal gold stripes at the left of the front; the drawing shows the stripes as hatching. They are not drawn.",
   "reason": "needs-photo",
   "scope": [
    "front"
   ],
   "wanted": "a larger photograph of the front's left end.",
   "what": "front-trim"
  },
  {
   "note": "The drawing shows two ears with two slots each at the front. The guides say only \"Rack mount kit\" and the page \"front and rear mounting hardware included\"; no document names the kit or places an ear along the depth.",
   "reason": "vendor-silent",
   "scope": [
    "front",
    "rear"
   ],
   "wanted": "the rack kit's part number, the ear positions and the rear brackets' size.",
   "what": "rack-ears"
  },
  {
   "note": "The network jacks' lamps, the module lamps and every label under the front connectors are not resolved at the size held. The system-ready lamp is drawn dark.",
   "reason": "needs-photo",
   "scope": [
    "front",
    "rear"
   ],
   "wanted": "a photograph of each face at a size where the lamps and labels read.",
   "what": "lamps-and-labels"
  }
 ],
